<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n104153" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τόθεν</span></b> , poet. Adv., answering to
		relat. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅθεν</span> and interrog. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πόθεν</span> (from <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">το-,</span> Demonstr. stem):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>thence,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hes.
				<u>Sc.</u>
				32
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Δρεπάνη τόθεν ἐκλήϊσται</span>
			<i>thence</i> it is called <i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.990
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅθεν,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pers.</u>
				99
			</span></i> (lyr.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>thereafter, thereupon,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Ag.</u>
				220
			</span></i> (lyr.); also <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐκ τόθεν,
			ἐξότε</span> . . <i>from the day when</i> . . , <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				4.520
			</span></i>.</div>
